## The open question the exploratory run must settle

Withholding drives SAFESTATE low. Whether PFM's XOR MASK does is still
unmeasured — and there is a tension: "contactors open at 5.5 s" is far
too late for a ~226 ms hardware safe state. Resolve it by sampling, with
one timestamp column each, relative to the injection write:
  latch bit, healthy flag, signature, FWDECNT, SAFESTATE (P10.7),
  physical contactor feedback (whatever line the driver reads back),
  software contactor state.
State explicitly which of the last two the earlier "5.5 s" observation
was. Expected if the mask reaches the SPI: FWDECNT climbing within one
heartbeat of the signature change, SAFESTATE LOW at ~226 ms, physical
contactor enable removed then, software contactor state following at
~5.5 s. Expected if it does NOT: FWDECNT flat, SAFESTATE HIGH, only the
5.5 s software path — that is a PR DEFECT (mask never reaches the SPI
write) and the single most important result this test can produce.
Report it as such; do not soften it.

